# Coach speech (Greek): the rules lesson (level 0, src/coach/lesson.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/lesson.lang.
#
# Placeholders: {your} / {my} = a piece of the player / of the coach ("ο πύργος σου", "ο ίππος μου"),
# with the forms of common.lang: {my:acc} (object, after με / μέχρι / προς), {my:se} (σε + article),
# {your:pron} "αυτός / αυτή / αυτό" ("{your:pron} είναι {your}." = "Αυτή είναι η βασίλισσά σου."),
# {my:pron_acc} "τον / την / το" ("Πάρ’ {my:pron_acc}!"), {my:pron_gen} "του / της", {your:os}
# (adjective ending, "καρφωμέν{your:os}"). {sq}, {sq2}, {to}, {esc} = squares, always "στο {sq}",
# "το {sq}", "από το {sq}"; {move} = a move. {@}, {@2}, {@3} are invisible marks: the coach points
# while saying the word right after the mark.
# A ".spoken" key is what the voice says instead: Latin file letters spelled the Greek way ("ε",
# "έιτς"), the letter "Γ" of the knight's move said "γάμμα", "Elo" said "Έλο".
# Files = στήλες, ranks = γραμμές, back rank = τελευταία γραμμή; the knight moves "σε σχήμα Γ", as
# Greek books say.

# ---- Chapter titles (said inside "Ας συνεχίσουμε με το κεφάλαιο «{chapter}».") -----------------------
# Headings with a capital first letter, quoted after "κεφάλαιο" (see event.lesson.* in events.lang).
